rs/paulobernardoaf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/paulobernardoaf","id":30026625,"login":"paulobernardoaf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMDI2NjI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/weni-ai/weni-webapp/commit/2e9dd151d64e55696c8249cf387f103f5cd0e5cc","node_id":"C_kwDOEqKwutoAKDJlOWRkMTUxZDY0ZTU1Njk2YzgyNDljZjM4N2YxMDNmNWNkMGU1Y2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/weni-ai/weni-webapp/commit/a30860907ca3145ee60ed81bf6ad3fd30a905f66","sha":"a30860907ca3145ee60ed81bf6ad3fd30a905f66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/weni-ai/weni-webapp/commits/a30860907ca3145ee60ed81bf6ad3fd30a905f66"}],"sha":"2e9dd151d64e55696c8249cf387f103f5cd0e5cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/weni-ai/weni-webapp/commits/2e9dd151d64e55696c8249cf387f103f5cd0e5cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30026625?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/paulobernardoaf","id":30026625,"login":"paulobernardoaf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMDI2NjI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/weni-ai/weni-webapp/commits/a30860907ca3145ee60ed81bf6ad3fd30a905f66/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T19:22:32Z","email":"paulo.bernardo@vtex.com","name":"Paulo Bernardo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T19:22:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add customer Okta login links and protect SSO settings (#1194)\n\n### Type of Change\n\n<!-- Select all that apply -->\n\n- [x] Feature\n- [ ] Bug fix\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [x] Tests\n- [ ] Chore\n- [x] Locales\n\n### Why\n\nEnterprise Okta login needs a customer-specific bookmark (door B) that\nstarts authentication against that company''s identity source, with no\nchooser in between. Blocked-organization copy still names only Google\nand Microsoft, which is wrong for Okta. The existing SSO form can also\nreplace or empty an allowlist it cannot represent. This ships the web\napp slice: door B, provider-agnostic copy, and read-only SSO guards.\nDoor B is not flag-gated. A well-formed `idp` always starts\nauthentication. Merge enables it. Runtime quality of the company-Okta\nleg still depends on Engine/infra (realm IdP alias and the\n`identity_provider` protocol mapper). Until the mapper lands, every\nlive-session door B entry re-authenticates with `prompt: ''login''`,\nwhich is correct per FR-008.\n\n### What Changed\n\n- **Door B** — `router.beforeEach` reads `idp`, validates\n`/^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{1,62}$/`, and calls `login({ idpHint, redirectUri })`.\nHostile identifiers degrade silently to door A. No new route, store,\nor dependency. No GrowthBook read.\n- **Redirect loop** — every door B `login()` passes `redirectUri` with\n`idp` stripped; session reuse strips it via `next()`. Mobile chats\nbounce also deletes `idp` from the packaged `redirect`.\n- **FR-008** — reuse only when `tokenParsed.identity_provider` equals\nthe identifier; mismatch / absent / empty / non-string passes\n`prompt: ''login''`. Signed-out branch passes no `prompt`.\n- **US3** — blocked-organization copy is provider-agnostic in en / pt_br\n/ es / ro. Unknown reasons render `orgs.access_disabled_reason.default`.\n`ssoConfig` is removed from OrgCard so identifiers cannot reach the UI.\n- **US4** — `isSsoReadOnly` when the allowlist has more than one entry\nor a value outside `[''google'', ''microsoft'']`. Three write guards:\ndisabled controls, `ssoDirty` forced false, and `saveChanges` skips\n`updateSSOConfig` even if the first two are bypassed (keep this skip;\nit is the one that survives a future combined SSO+2FA save).\n- **US5** — Sentry `entry_door` tag is one of `default` |\n`direct_start` | `direct_start_rejected`. Never the identifier.\n- Tests for the router guard, identifier table (R1–R21, A1–A2),\n`prompt: ''login''`, loop prevention, locale parity, OrgCard/orgList,\nand UpdateOrg read-only matrix. `UpdateOrgSSO.spec.js` is unmodified\n(FR-018 / SC-010).\nSpec: `specs/001-okta-login-webapp/`\n\n### Diagram\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  A[Navigation with ?idp=] --> B{Syntactic validation}\n  B -->|rejected or absent| C[Door A: login with no idpHint]\n  B -->|accepted| D{Authenticated?}\n  D -->|no| E[\"login({ idpHint, redirectUri minus idp })\"]\n  D -->|yes| F{identity_provider equals idp?}\n  F -->|yes| G[\"next() with idp stripped\"]\n  F -->|no / unknown| H[\"login({ idpHint, prompt: ''login'', redirectUri minus idp })\"]\n```\n\n### <!-- (optional) -->\n\n<!-- Include screenshots, GIFs or videos when applicable. -->","tree":{"sha":"fbcc66bf2ccbc05f9c9fb4c4256e720e1c043755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/weni-ai/weni-webapp/git/trees/fbcc66bf2ccbc05f9c9fb4c4256e720e1c043755"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/weni-ai/weni-webapp/git/commits/a30860907ca3145ee60ed81bf6ad3fd30a905f66","verification":{"payload":"tree fbcc66bf2ccbc05f9c9fb4c4256e720e1c043755\nparent 3fd3e0a4a3046dd676537117a4f05fa07b5fe8af\nparent c21164ec01ab3eb425bb02c2423c3c434133609f\nauthor Paulo Bernardo <paulo.bernardo@vtex.com> 1788895352 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788895352 -0300\n\nfeat: add customer Okta login links and protect SSO settings (#1194)\n\n### Type of Change\n\n<!-- Select all that apply -->\n\n- [x] Feature\n- [ ] Bug fix\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [x] Tests\n- [ ] Chore\n- [x] Locales\n\n### Why\n\nEnterprise Okta login needs a customer-specific bookmark (door B) that\nstarts authentication against that company''s identity source, with no\nchooser in between. Blocked-organization copy still names only Google\nand Microsoft, which is wrong for Okta. The existing SSO form can also\nreplace or empty an allowlist it cannot represent. This ships the web\napp slice: door B, provider-agnostic copy, and read-only SSO guards.\nDoor B is not flag-gated. A well-formed `idp` always starts\nauthentication. Merge enables it. Runtime quality of the company-Okta\nleg still depends on Engine/infra (realm IdP alias and the\n`identity_provider` protocol mapper). Until the mapper lands, every\nlive-session door B entry re-authenticates with `prompt: ''login''`,\nwhich is correct per FR-008.\n\n### What Changed\n\n- **Door B** — `router.beforeEach` reads `idp`, validates\n`/^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{1,62}$/`, and calls `login({ idpHint, redirectUri })`.\nHostile identifiers degrade silently to door A. No new route, store,\nor dependency. No GrowthBook read.\n- **Redirect loop** — every door B `login()` passes `redirectUri` with\n`idp` stripped; session reuse strips it via `next()`. Mobile chats\nbounce also deletes `idp` from the packaged `redirect`.\n- **FR-008** — reuse only when `tokenParsed.identity_provider` equals\nthe identifier; mismatch / absent / empty / non-string passes\n`prompt: ''login''`. Signed-out branch passes no `prompt`.\n- **US3** — blocked-organization copy is provider-agnostic in en / pt_br\n/ es / ro. Unknown reasons render `orgs.access_disabled_reason.default`.\n`ssoConfig` is removed from OrgCard so identifiers cannot reach the UI.\n- **US4** — `isSsoReadOnly` when the allowlist has more than one entry\nor a value outside `[''google'', ''microsoft'']`. Three write guards:\ndisabled controls, `ssoDirty` forced false, and `saveChanges` skips\n`updateSSOConfig` even if the first two are bypassed (keep this skip;\nit is the one that survives a future combined SSO+2FA save).\n- **US5** — Sentry `entry_door` tag is one of `default` |\n`direct_start` | `direct_start_rejected`. Never the identifier.\n- Tests for the router guard, identifier table (R1–R21, A1–A2),\n`prompt: ''login''`, loop prevention, locale parity, OrgCard/orgList,\nand UpdateOrg read-only matrix. `UpdateOrgSSO.spec.js` is unmodified\n(FR-018 / SC-010).\nSpec: `specs/001-okta-login-webapp/`\n\n### Diagram\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  A[Navigation with ?idp=] --> B{Syntactic validation}\n  B -->|rejected or absent| C[Door A: login with no idpHint]\n  B -->|accepted| D{Authenticated?}\n  D -->|no| E[\"login({ idpHint, redirectUri minus idp })\"]\n  D -->|yes| F{identity_provider equals idp?}\n  F -->|yes| G[\"next() with idp stripped\"]\n  F -->|no / unknown| H[\"login({ idpHint, prompt: ''login'', redirectUri minus idp })\"]\n```\n\n### <!-- (optional) -->\n\n<!-- Include screenshots, GIFs or videos when applicable. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoGB4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkiIQAA/nxsGQEl3tEIB62R0te3fV\n7rOH2YHmH2wbrxlaWlvjyOYKGjwiIt+tedFc0H1KwT0FThoqnbPydz25aZx4m6PL\nvyIA