anizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/weni-ai/weni-webapp/commits/adb84579d89c0f8ec6a15102d3f1b053080722e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T14:51:12Z","email":"paulo.bernardo@vtex.com","name":"Paulo Bernardo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T12:18:16Z","email":"30026625+paulobernardoaf@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Paulo Bernardo"},"message":"refactor: migrate project management from Vuex to Pinia\n\n- Transitioned project management from Vuex to a new Pinia store, enhancing state management and reactivity.\n- Updated components to utilize the new Pinia store, including methods for handling projects and their related data.\n- Removed legacy Vuex actions and integrated new Pinia actions for project functionality.\n- Added unit tests for the new project store to ensure proper functionality and reliability.","tree":{"sha":"5544e720a4782889f79ec763f23b69d210f4ab3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/weni-ai/weni-webapp/git/trees/5544e720a4782889f79ec763f23b69d210f4ab3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/weni-ai/weni-webapp/git/commits/adb84579d89c0f8ec6a15102d3f1b053080722e5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30026625?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/paulobernardoaf","id":30026625,"login":"paulobernardoaf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMDI2NjI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/weni-ai/weni-webapp/commit/adb84579d89c0f8ec6a15102d3f1b053080722e5","node_id":"C_kwDOEqKwutoAKGFkYjg0NTc5ZDg5YzBmOGVjNmExNTEwMmQzZjFiMDUzMDgwNzIyZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/weni-ai/weni-webapp/commit/a9bbdde7ce3177365b45d34598ddff52bb51f275","sha":"a9bbdde7ce3177365b45d34598ddff52bb51f275","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/weni-ai/weni-webapp/commits/a9bbdde7ce3177365b45d34598ddff52bb51f275"}],"sha":"adb84579d89c0f8ec6a15102d3f1b053080722e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/weni-ai/weni-webapp/commits/adb84579d89c0f8ec6a15102d3f1b053080722e5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30026625?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/paulobernardoaf","id":30026625,"login":"paulobernardoaf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMDI2NjI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/paulobernardoaf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/weni-ai/weni-webapp/commits/a9bbdde7ce3177365b45d34598ddff52bb51f275/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T12:16:31Z","email":"paulo.bernardo@vtex.com","name":"Paulo Bernardo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T12:16:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: migrate organization management from Vuex to Pinia (#1189)\n\n### Type of Change\n- [ ] Feature\n- [ ] Bug fix\n- [x] Refactor\n- [x] Tests\n- [ ] Chore\n- [ ] Locales\n\n### Why\nThe `Org` module was previously managed as a Vuex module, which required accessing state via `this.$store.state.Org`, `this.$store.getters`, and dispatching actions through Vuex. Migrating it to a Pinia store aligns it with the rest of the application''s state management direction, removes the dependency on the global Vuex store for org-related data, and makes the store easier to test and consume directly in components.\n\n### What Changed\nThe `Org` Vuex module (`state.js`, `mutations.js`, `getters.js`, `actions.js`) was replaced with a single Pinia store defined in `src/store/org/index.js` using the Composition API style (`defineStore` with a setup function).\n\nAll components and views that previously accessed org state via `this.$store.state.Org.*`, `this.$store.getters.currentOrg`, or `this.$store.getters.org` now import and use `useOrgStore()` directly. Actions such as `setCurrentOrg`, `clearCurrentOrg`, `getOrg`, `getOrgs`, `getNextOrgs`, `removeOrgFromList`, `leaveOrg`, `removeAuthorization`, `changeAuthorization`, `editOrg`, `deleteOrg`, and others were moved from Vuex `mapActions` to Pinia `mapPiniaActions`. The `Org` module was removed from the Vuex store''s module registry.\n\nThe `org` computed getter (previously a Vuex getter resolving the org from route params) is now a `computed` inside the Pinia store. The `featureFlags` store and `growthbook` utility were updated to read `currentOrg` from the Pinia store instead of Vuex state.\n\nTests across components and views were updated to use `createTestingPinia` with `initialState.Org` instead of Vuex state/getters, and action assertions were updated to reference `useOrgStore()` mock functions directly. A new dedicated test file `src/store/org/__tests__/org.spec.js` was added with full coverage of the store''s state, getters, mutations, and actions.\n\n### Diagram\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[Components / Views] -->|useOrgStore| B[Pinia Org Store]\n    B --> C[orgsApi]\n    B --> D[router - currentRoute]\n    B --> E[rootStore - Project state]\n    F[Vuex Store] -->|Project module only| G[Project State]\n    A -->|mapGetters / mapActions| F\n```","tree":{"sha":"3a35005ea179f7f1cac51b3cdd467938423531a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/weni-ai/weni-webapp/git/trees/3a35005ea179f7f1cac51b3cdd467938423531a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/weni-ai/weni-webapp/git/commits/a9bbdde7ce3177365b45d34598ddff52bb51f275","verification":{"payload":"tree 3a35005ea179f7f1cac51b3cdd467938423531a8\nparent 91c7b1ba0bb3de4abf89489c0b21f76e70869b96\nparent a5adfa4cd83cdd7b974536202add23300eb4e86a\nauthor Paulo Bernardo <paulo.bernardo@vtex.com> 1787919391 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787919391 -0300\n\nrefactor: migrate organization management from Vuex to Pinia (#1189)\n\n### Type of Change\n- [ ] Feature\n- [ ] Bug fix\n- [x] Refactor\n- [x] Tests\n- [ ] Chore\n- [ ] Locales\n\n### Why\nThe `Org` module was previously managed as a Vuex module, which required accessing state via `this.$store.state.Org`, `this.$store.getters`, and dispatching actions through Vuex. Migrating it to a Pinia store aligns it with the rest of the application''s state management direction, removes the dependency on the global Vuex store for org-related data, and makes the store easier to test and consume directly in components.\n\n### What Changed\nThe `Org` Vuex module (`state.js`, `mutations.js`, `getters.js`, `actions.js`) was replaced with a single Pinia store defined in `src/store/org/index.js` using the Composition API style (`defineStore` with a setup function).\n\nAll components and views that previously accessed org state via `this.$store.state.Org.*`, `this.$store.getters.currentOrg`, or `this.$store.getters.org` now import and use `useOrgStore()` directly. Actions such as `setCurrentOrg`, `clearCurrentOrg`, `getOrg`, `getOrgs`, `getNextOrgs`, `removeOrgFromList`, `leaveOrg`, `removeAuthorization`, `changeAuthorization`, `editOrg`, `deleteOrg`, and others were moved from Vuex `mapActions` to Pinia `mapPiniaActions`. The `Org` module was removed from the Vuex store''s module registry.\n\nThe `org` computed getter (previously a Vuex getter resolving the org from route params) is now a `computed` inside the Pinia store. The `featureFlags` store and `growthbook` utility were updated to read `currentOrg` from the Pinia store instead of Vuex state.\n\nTests across components and views were updated to use `createTestingPinia` with `initialState.Org` instead of Vuex state/getters, and action assertions were updated to reference `useOrgStore()` mock functions directly. A new dedicated test file `src/store/org/__tests__/org.spec.js` was added with full coverage of the store''s state, getters, mutations, and actions.\n\n### Diagram\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[Components / Views] -->|useOrgStore| B[Pinia Org Store]\n    B --> C[orgsApi]\n    B --> D[router - currentRoute]\n    B --> E[rootStore - Project state]\n    F[Vuex Store] -->|Project module only| G[Project State]\n    A -->|mapGetters / mapActions| F\n```","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkXwfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeksQAG4fQYRUitQDfoFotC/gPdXC\n8O1qnjWjDMqMGN+Lk7j+Gf3D+5L3cqn+YfhWEVd5bo4wgGxWEeIaAHJjkbt3fHrt\nuzWtcboAk52L0I1mIG1WnZWrkHJDV9Ifnm/CZ51n3/NCpCPPNsSshIuWLD9eDJmn\nVW3pxAEqEL4Elth297UoPRo0W2L8/iFFs9tUJKp/IyTPd8mhpOhaBpxQHjXzPGFq\nn9LHt5heAYbNTgxFfU/Rtr0PJ6OfpI1gERz1CE9Unuy5cwnNxlHOkLPJtS4Ek4SD\n1BYZ0ncVEog/l17r/wPdUhB2jPpZFzIQZbATV7E5pnHG0BVqNBuTo8D4Nvk6nw4g\nG3al93xk2kynfPBXUJ2bqzcq6BwUn4+Ke/RPSSKsvAkjVlAaCoxdmcUr/SyYtTm3\nGArIe7mxPB5Tzm+zDD12LGe01VzLNJ4pAt4rTbmfe3puTOImYUrnLafzFPu82b3a\nGTL3V5HbrZnm1ne1C5Ncich7rNbtwjeJDOh9DPejuEJpNQZosRu0Z/gjWwOXuwAd\ngzpR14IccH0Dhfk9TY018TtJCMLmPj6iJv8gSMgfib2BNSXPHAyGpbgCnyPZiQhj\nC6HJqEGpWzrcqOI3zQDQ0bmLFE3QL3/AnrqtN6uUXMPLpFae27nytgJfR/vw71CB\nKUtQhqQhCy6cEQt/i8MV\n=daH+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T12:16:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/weni-ai/weni-webapp/commit/a9bbdde7ce3177365b45d34598ddff52bb51f275","node_id":"C_kwDOEqKwutoAKGE5YmJkZGU3Y2UzMTc