The `BillingSteps` store was implemented as a Vuex module, which is inconsistent with the rest of the codebase''s migration toward Pinia. Keeping it in Vuex also required components to access state directly via `this.$store.state.BillingSteps.*`, making the code harder to maintain and test.\n\n### What Changed\n- Converted the `BillingSteps` Vuex module (state, mutations, actions) into a Pinia store using the Composition API (`defineStore` with `ref`/`reactive`).\n- Removed the `BillingSteps` module from the Vuex store and deleted the separate `state.js`, `mutations.js`, and `actions.js` files.\n- Updated all components and views that previously accessed `this.$store.state.BillingSteps.*` to use `BillingStepsStore` via `mapStores(useBillingStepsStore)`.\n- Replaced `mapActions([''setBillingStep''])` Vuex calls with `mapPiniaActions(useBillingStepsStore, [''setBillingStep''])` in `WarningMaxActiveContacts.vue`, `billing.vue`, and `FormAddress.vue`.\n- Updated existing unit tests for `FormAddress`, `FormCreditCard`, `Modal`, `WarningMaxActiveContacts`, and `billing` to use Pinia instead of a mocked Vuex store.\n- Added a comprehensive unit test suite for `useBillingStepsStore` covering initial state, org/members/project step actions, modal step actions, integration count management, pricing plan fetching, billing detail setters, and setup intent handling.","tree":{"sha":"aa38d593d8a27c49063798dd150be7743e754917","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/weni-ai/weni-webapp/git/trees/aa38d593d8a27c49063798dd150be7743e754917"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/weni-ai/weni-webapp/git/commits/91c7b1ba0bb3de4abf89489c0b21f76e70869b96","verification":{"payload":"tree aa38d593d8a27c49063798dd150be7743e754917\nparent cc98cd2497c125b85f7f97a9ba1cb3aa53449dee\nparent 592de75c8bce2bfe55c1f1c4a4073cb77107aec3\nauthor Paulo Bernardo <paulo.bernardo@vtex.com> 1787919213 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787919213 -0300\n\nrefactor: migrate billing steps management from Vuex to Pinia (#1188)\n\n### Type of Change\n- [ ] Feature\n- [ ] Bug fix\n- [x] Refactor\n- [x] Tests\n- [ ] Chore\n- [ ] Locales\n\n### Why\nThe `BillingSteps` store was implemented as a Vuex module, which is inconsistent with the rest of the codebase''s migration toward Pinia. Keeping it in Vuex also required components to access state directly via `this.$store.state.BillingSteps.*`, making the code harder to maintain and test.\n\n### What Changed\n- Converted the `BillingSteps` Vuex module (state, mutations, actions) into a Pinia store using the Composition API (`defineStore` with `ref`/`reactive`).\n- Removed the `BillingSteps` module from the Vuex store and deleted the separate `state.js`, `mutations.js`, and `actions.js` files.\n- Updated all components and views that previously accessed `this.$store.state.BillingSteps.*` to use `BillingStepsStore` via `mapStores(useBillingStepsStore)`.\n- Replaced `mapActions([''setBillingStep''])` Vuex calls with `mapPiniaActions(useBillingStepsStore, [''setBillingStep''])` in `WarningMaxActiveContacts.vue`, `billing.vue`, and `FormAddress.vue`.\n- Updated existing unit tests for `FormAddress`, `FormCreditCard`, `Modal`, `WarningMaxActiveContacts`, and `billing` to use Pinia instead of a mocked Vuex store.\n- Added a comprehensive unit test suite for `useBillingStepsStore` covering initial state, org/members/project step actions, modal step actions, integration count management, pricing plan fetching, billing detail setters, and setup intent handling.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkXttCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9a0QABpcNGCUqPGko8dornx7KAnb\niXXaqVahqu4F2BZNgocIAr3GURUM+/emMcWUtqIisGxmTniXVaUDFRxH3axpU88X\nnTn/w3ZgqCzzggpOvxbrERTW1ln1epu+0DMSZqopisWV0i5M4MLNF6d7KjmfHIvt\nB9sER2sFN7dz6sgcTJ2S11S40jJPU25t6u7cqqOdbZyR5DNpwyqRBxreLMDW1Z4W\n0i1c7Wmet+t6tNLlkKnCxPW+gRuBNUMwnq4wlTwOVVJgMio2IwM6lQW+xu0I426T\n0fIpF5gK8tK3jlfBkpj3hAFzLq6kr8PZF7a5Rl2wG+5nPN/uqCDwRwFWHLMu1gIG\ngQ8OzQsTFZlgsw2AuBH5Vs0D